From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Market Canopy <office@marketcanopy.invalid>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Sign in to Market Canopy from the start screen

The start screen shows the Market Canopy account the native account
module keeps (desktop-sdk patch 0002): Sign in to Market Canopy opens the
system browser, then the signed-in person, the organization picker,
Update required or offline. Market Canopy's cloud connection is made by
native code after sign-in, so there is no connect step. Window focus
asks the module to read the credential store again (P02 contract 5.4).

Both shells hand every launch argument and opened link to the module
first (CallCommand "mc:scheme:"), so a sign-in callback forwarded by the
single-instance check, or a link that carries a credential, is never
opened as a document.
